\p
\v 1 \add Each year, honour\add* your god Yahweh \add ≈in the¦89805 early spring\add* by celebrating the¦89806 ‘pass-over¦89808’, because¦89811 it was one night¦89818 \add ≈in¦89812 the early spring\add* that \add *he\add* brought¦89814 you¦89814 out¦89814 of¦89816 Egypt¦89817 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*.\x + \xo 16:1-8: \xt Exo 12:1-20; Lev 23:5-8; Num 28:16-25.\x*
\v 2 ⇔\add ≈In¦89826 order to celebrate, go to\add* the place¦89826 that your god¦89823 Yahweh¦89830 will¦89829 choose¦89829 \add ≈to¦89831 attach his¦89832 name¦89832 to\add*, and there¦89833 sacrifice¦89820 to¦89822 \add *him\add* one \add young\add* animal from your flock¦89824 or herd¦89825.
\v 3 Don't¦89835 eat¦89837 any leavened¦89839 bread with it¦89838. For seven¦89840 days¦89841, you¦89842 must¦89842 eat¦89842 flat¦89845 bread¦89845 (the bread¦89846 of¦89846 suffering¦89847) because¦89848 you¦89850 came¦89850 out¦89850 of¦89851 Egypt¦89852 in a rush¦89849. That's¦89853 how you¦89854 should¦89854 remember¦89854 the¦89860 day¦89860 of¦89860 your¦89861 exit from¦89862 Egypt¦89863 for the¦89865 rest of¦89865 your¦89866 life¦89866.
\v 4 \add In fact,\add* for¦89871 seven¦89876 days¦89877 you shouldn't¦89878 even have any¦89881 rising agent within your borders¦89875, and none of¦89875 the¦89883 meat¦89883 from the sacrifice¦89885 on that¦89884 first¦89888 evening¦89886 is allowed to be left¦89880 until the¦89887 morning¦89889.
\p
\v 5 You¦89892 mustn't sacrifice¦89893 the¦89896 ‘pass-over¦89896’ \add animal\add* within any of¦89897 your¦89898 towns that¦89899 your¦89898 god¦89902 Yahweh¦89901 is¦89903 giving¦89903 to¦89904 you¦89904—
\v 6 only at the¦89911 place¦89911 that¦89912 your¦89916 god¦89916 Yahweh¦89915 will¦89914 choose¦89914 to¦89917 \add ≈attach his¦89918 name¦89918 to\add*. That's where you¦89920 must¦89920 sacrifice¦89920 the¦89923 ‘pass-over¦89923’ \add animal\add* at sunset, which¦89912 was the¦89927 time¦89927 when \add ≈your¦89928 ancestors\add* started leaving Egypt¦89929.
\v 7 You¦89931 must¦89931 cook¦89931 the meat and¦89932 eat¦89932 it at the place¦89933 that¦89934 Yahweh¦89936 will¦89935 choose¦89935, then¦89939 in¦89940 the morning¦89940 you¦89941 can \add start\add* returning to¦89942 your¦89942 \add ≈homes¦89942\add*.
\v 8 Then for six¦89944 days¦89945 you¦89946 must¦89946 only eat¦89946 flat¦89947 bread¦89947, and¦89948 the¦89949 seventh¦89949 day is a special celebration for¦89951 your¦89952 god¦89952 Yahweh¦89951—don't¦89953 do¦89954 any work¦89955 on that day.
