\v 20 \add ≈However,\add* if¦92635 \add @the¦92638 accusation¦92638\add* was¦92638 true¦92637 and the young woman¦92645 \add ≈hadn't been¦92643 a virgin¦92644\add*,
\v 21 then¦92648 they¦92648 must¦92648 take¦92648 \add *her\add* to¦92653 the¦92655 doorway¦92655 of her¦92658 father's¦92658 house. Then¦92659 the¦92660 men¦92660 from that city¦92661 must \add ≈execute her¦92661 by throwing rocks¦92662 at her\add*, because¦92664 she's¦92666 done¦92666 a¦92667 disgraceful¦92667 thing in¦92668 Yisrael¦92668—committing fornication \add ≈while she still lived in\add* her¦92671 father's¦92671 house. That's how you'll¦92672 remove¦92672 evil¦92673 from¦92674 \add ≈your¦92674 country\add*.
