\p
\v 25 If¦92761 the¦92765 man¦92765 found¦92764 the¦92768 young¦92768 woman¦92768 \add out\add* in the¦92770 countryside¦92763 and¦92771 \add ≈overpowers\add* her¦92773 and¦92775 \add ≈rapes\add* her¦92776, then¦92777 the¦92778 man¦92778 \add ≈must be¦92783 executed\add*
\v 26 but¦92785 don't¦92789 do¦92791 anything¦92792 to¦92794 that woman¦92794 because¦92798 she's not worthy of¦92796 death¦92797. (This¦92809 is¦92807 similar to the case of a man murdering¦92805 another man \add out in the countryside\add*.)
\v 27 When that man found¦92813 her¦92813 \add out\add* in the countryside¦92812, then she¦92814 would have cried¦92814 out \add for help\add*, but¦92818 no \add ≈one was there¦92818 to¦92820 save\add* her¦92820.
