\p
\v 9 When¦93038 \add @your warriors\add* are out¦93033 besieging your¦93037 enemies¦93037, they you must avoid \add ≈ceremonial impurity\add*.
\v 10 If¦93044 something happens¦93054 at night¦93056 to make a¦93048 man¦93048 ‘unclean’, then¦93057 he¦93057 must¦93057 stay outside¦93057 the¦93060 camp¦93061 \add the next day\add* \add ≈and not¦93062 join the others\add*.
\v 11 That evening¦93073, he¦93074 must¦93074 wash¦93074 himself in water¦93075, then¦93076 once the¦93077 sun¦93077 has set, he¦93078 may reenter the¦93082 camp¦93082.
\p
\v 12 You must have a¦93086 place outside¦93089 your camp¦93090 where you¦93091 can go¦93091 to¦93092 \add relieve yourself\add*.
\v 13 You must have a¦93096 spade¦93096 among your¦93101 equipment¦93101 so¦93102 that when¦93103 you¦93103 go to relieve yourself, you¦93105 can dig¦93105 a hole and¦93107 then¦93108 cover¦93108 it up afterwards,
\v 14 because¦93114 your¦93116 god¦93116 Yahweh¦93115 walks¦93117 in¦93119 your¦93120 camp¦93120 to¦93121 give¦93121 you¦93121 victory \add ≈to¦93122 defeat\add* your¦93123 enemies¦93123, so your¦93124 camp must be sacred¦93127 so¦93128 he¦93130 won't¦93128 see¦93130 anything ‘unclean’ and¦93134 turn¦93134 away from¦93135 you¦93135.
\s1 Various regulations
