\v 17 Don't¦93636 pervert justice¦93638 if it involves foreigners¦93639 or orphans¦93640, and¦93641 don't¦93641 take¦93642 a¦93644 widow's¦93644 cloak as security \add for a loan\add*.\x + \xo 24:17-18: \xt Exo 23:9; Lev 19:33-34; Deu 27:19.\x*
\v 18 Remember¦93646 that¦93647 you were a¦93648 slave¦93648 in¦93650 Egypt¦93650 and¦93651 your¦93653 god¦93653 Yahweh¦93652 \add ≈rescued\add* you from¦93654 there¦93654. \add ≈That's why\add* I'm¦93658 commanding¦93659 you¦93659 to do¦93660 those \add #things¦93663\add*—\add ≈to be considerate about helping other people who are in need\add*.
\p
\v 19 When you¦93668 \add ≈harvest your crops\add*, if¦93667 you¦93671 forget¦93671 a¦93672 tied bundle in¦93673 your field¦93673, don't¦93674 go back to¦93676 get¦93676 it¦93676—it'll¦93680 be for a \add resident\add* foreigner¦93677 or an orphan or widow¦93679 \add to pick up\add*,\x + \xo 24:19-21: \xt Lev 19:9-10; 23:22.\x* so¦93681 that¦93681 your¦93684 god¦93684 Yahweh¦93683 can bless¦93682 everything \add ≈that you¦93682 do\add*.
